title: CRLF Injection / HTTP Response Splitting
id: 91f666d0-0eb1-4366-bf4c-fd7dac2a6734
status: experimental
description: Detects CRLF injection attempts where encoded carriage-return/line-feed sequences (%0d%0a) are used to inject headers or split the HTTP response, enabling cache poisoning and header manipulation.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/
logsource:
  category: webserver
detection:
  selection:
    cs-uri-query|contains:
      - '%0d%0a'
      - '%0D%0A'
      - '\r\nSet-Cookie'
      - '%0aSet-Cookie'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - cs-uri-query
  - cs-uri-stem
  - c-ip
falsepositives:
  - Rare legitimate encoded newlines
level: medium
tags:
  - attack.initial_access
  - attack.t1190
